{
  "about": "Production per faction (2026-11-28). Each faction: `slots` (hand-edited) maps the map tier slots — hq, t1–t3, a tier split into branches with a letter (t2a, t2b) — to its CoH3 production buildings; `tier2` is its Tier 2 building (non-tank support vehicles: trucks, ambulances, medical half-tracks); `buildings` is written by `node tools/coh3/production.js` from CoH3 spawner data (as coh3stats' explorer lists it), each with three unlock lists: `base` (produced from the start), `doctrine` (unlocked by a doctrine: CoH3 battlegroup units and doctrine conversions' targets), `research` (researched in that building: heroes, heavy armour and pricier variants no CoH3 building makes, research conversions' targets). The HQ makes only base engineers and recon units; mid-game engineers come from tier buildings. Hand overrides for any squad: `place` (squad → building), `unlock` (squad → base / doctrine / research). Only squads present in the unit data are offered.",
